    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for LawDog centers on two high-upside plays against Dobnak: **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Zack Gelof** (60.47). **Lawrence Butler** headlines our unit today; the 17% SP Skill bump from the Dobnak matchup, paired with a solid #4 order slot, makes him our most efficient producer. We are also leaning heavily on **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (69.84), who remains an anchor despite a tougher matchup, and **Daulton Varsho** (68.66). **Daulton Varsho** is particularly well-positioned against Rodriguez due to a favorable dynamic platoon advantage (+10%), offering a significant ceiling boost in a game where efficiency is paramount.\n\nThe toughest decision of the day involved the utility slot, where **Braden Montgomery** (53.25) narrowly edged out others to secure a start. While **JJ Bleday** (51.44) and **Dylan Beavers** (54.79) are active, their scores fluctuate based on park factors and opponent talent\u2014specifically, **Dylan Beavers** benefits from a massive 16% park boost against Cole, though he faces the stiffest competition among our starters today in terms of individual pitcher skill. **Cal Raleigh** (0.00) remains the most notable bench piece; while his base metrics are strong enough to contribute, he is currently sidelined, leaving us to rely on our active depth to maintain our standing in the critical stolen base category. \n\nWe are monitoring several risk factors closely. **Jung Hoo Lee** (43.28) faces a daunting matchup against Williams, who carries an elite 2.99 xERA, significantly dragging down his production potential. Furthermore, we are operating without the services of **Bryce Harper**, **Will Smith** (currently on the IL), and **Justin Crawford**, which forces us to maximize the output of **Jonathan Aranda** (69.45) at 1B. We expect **Jonathan Aranda** to capitalize on the 5.08 xERA of Bieber, as his recency and SP-skill adjustment (+19%) represent the highest efficiency gain of any player in today\u2019s 